<title>NETHERLANDS: GERMAN CITY DETAILS 1996 STOCK DIVIDEND.</title>
<headline>GERMAN CITY DETAILS 1996 STOCK DIVIDEND.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>German City Estates , an Amsterdam quoted property company, said on Thursday it had set the stock alternative to its 1996 dividend at one new share for every 25 shares already held.</p>
<p>In March, German City Estates announced it would pay a 1996 cash dividend of 0.90 guilders per share, up from 0.80 guilders.</p>
<p>German City shares closed at 27.60 guilders on the Amsterdam Stock Exchange on Wednesday, and will start trading ex-dividend today.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000 (fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
